window.EN={"1":"Pursuing the Bern army's Ilia garrison force, Roy and the Etrurian army","2":"set foot into a great ruin located a short distance from Edessa.","3":"This place dates back to the \"Scouring,\" and putting together the accounts of the locals and the like,","4":"it seemed extremely likely that one of the \"Divine Weapons\" existed here.","5":"Lord Tick! The enemy, the enemy is closing in!","6":"There's no need to panic. This place is surrounded by walls two and three layers deep.","7":"They can't force their way in that easily.","8":"B-but, sir...","9":"The enemy has utterly crushed Ilia's own army and our allied forces, every one of them!","10":"For us alone to win is...","11":"There's no need to win.","12":"General Murdock said it would be enough for us just to hold this place.","13":"We need only defend firmly and let it pass us by. Understood?","14":"※If Zelot is deployed","15":"So this is where a \"Divine Weapon\" is...","16":"Lord Zelot, did you know about this place?","17":"I'd heard of it. As for the \"Divine Weapon\" here, at least a little...","18":"What kind of weapon is it?","19":"It's said to have been used by Barigan, who was praised as \"the knight among knights.\"","20":"The \"Icewater Spear,\" Marte.","21":"If it's about Barigan, I know the story well.","22":"His name always comes up as a model of knighthood when learning about war.","23":"...By the way, this building, no matter which way you turn, is nothing but walls...","24":"There doesn't seem to be a path leading further in.","25":"The remaining Bern soldiers guarding this place must have filled in the passage.","26":"...If it was done in a hurry, it might be fragile, then.","27":"That's right. Probably so.","28":"Understood. Let's try what we can.","29":"※If Zelot is not deployed, and Juno is deployed","30":"So this is where a \"Divine Weapon\" is...","31":"Lady Juno, did you know about this place?","32":"I'd heard of it. As for the \"Divine Weapon\" here, at least a little...","33":"What kind of weapon is it?","34":"It's said to have been used by Barigan, who was praised as \"the knight among knights.\"","35":"The \"Icewater Spear,\" Marte.","36":"If it's about Barigan, I know the story well.","37":"His name always comes up as a model of knighthood when learning about war.","38":"...By the way, this building, no matter which way you turn, is nothing but walls...","39":"There doesn't seem to be a path leading further in.","40":"Surely the remaining Bern soldiers guarding this place","41":"must have filled in the passage.","42":"...If it was done in a hurry, it might be fragile...","43":"That's certainly a possibility.","44":"Understood. Let's try what we can.","45":"※If Zelot and Juno are not deployed","46":"So this is where a \"Divine Weapon\" is...","47":"Elffin, was anything about this place recorded anywhere?","48":"Yes. It seems the \"Icewater Spear,\" Marte, is hidden here.","49":"The \"Icewater Spear\"...","50":"It's said to have been used by Barigan, who was praised as \"the knight among knights.\"","51":"I see, if it's about Barigan, I know the story well.","52":"His name always comes up as a model of knighthood when learning about war.","53":"...By the way, this building, no matter which way you turn, is nothing but walls...","54":"There doesn't seem to be a path leading further in.","55":"Surely the remaining Bern soldiers guarding this place","56":"must have filled in the passage.","57":"...If it was done in a hurry, it might be fragile...","58":"That's certainly a possibility.","59":"Understood. Let's try what we can.","60":"Impossible... am I dreaming?","61":"How in the world did they get past that wall...?","62":"...Go on ahead, worthy one.","63":"And know this: Bern's true power...","64":"We found it! A spear, beneath the throne!","65":".........","66":"So this is... the \"Icewater Spear\" Barigan used, Marte.","67":"Just as its name says, it gleams silver-white—a magnificent spear.","68":"Lord Roy.","69":"It seems the Bern soldiers who were elsewhere in the ruins are fleeing.","70":"I see.","71":"\"I see\" isn't good enough. We must pursue them.","72":"No.","73":"They're trying to get away from the battlefield. They surely have no more will to fight.","74":"But still...","75":"Soldiers have families too. There's no need to fight them more than necessary.","76":"Princess Guinevere, we'll finally be advancing our army into Bern's homeland. Before that, though...","77":"...You mean about my brother, don't you.","78":"...At the time, Prince Zephiel, as heir to Bern,","79":"had grown up splendidly, hadn't he.","80":"So I've heard.","81":"Even so, Bern's former king came to resent Prince Zephiel, didn't he?","82":"Rather... it's because my brother had grown so remarkably.","83":"Eh...","84":"My father, Bern's former king, was, as a king, a man of ordinary talent, they say.","85":"So my brother's outstanding talent seems to have only made Father's feelings all the colder.","86":".........","87":"And then, one day at last, Father is said to have called my brother and told him:","88":"\"Someone fit for it shall be brought in to marry Guinevere, and he shall take the throne of Bern.\"","89":"What...! ...That's too much!","90":"Even so, my brother is said to have answered then that if that was how it was, so be it.","91":"But to my brother, who everyone expected to be the next king, those around him would not allow such a thing.","92":"And so, Father, driven to distraction...","93":"...Plotted to assassinate Prince Zephiel?","94":"...At a drinking banquet, my brother was handed a poisoned cup directly by our father the king.","95":"And that, it's said, was the first and last cup he ever received from Father...","96":"After returning to his room, my brother began to suffer,","97":"and for more than ten days after that, he is said to have hovered between life and death.","98":"He was sheltered by General Murdock, who had raised him,","99":"and somehow, my brother's life was spared.","100":"...Did Father do nothing after that?","101":"...No.","102":"He treated General Murdock, who had saved my brother, and my brother's mother as obstacles too,","103":"and is said to have schemed to do away with my brother along with them.","104":"My brother, still bedridden with illness, learned of this and feigned his own death...","105":"and when Father came to confirm my brother's death, from within the coffin... with a sword...","106":".........","107":"...At the time, I was still young, and had no way of understanding such circumstances.","108":"All I understood was that from that day—the day Father died—onward, my brother's face lost its smile.","109":"Until then, he could be strict, but he was a warm, gentle brother. That's why...","110":"Princess Guinevere...","111":"That's why, deep in my heart, I believed my brother hadn't changed.","112":"That someday, surely, he would return to being the kind Zephiel brother he once was.","113":"I believed that... I kept believing that, all along...","114":"I see, so that's how it was...","115":"...But now, my brother is somewhere my voice can no longer reach.","116":"Lord Roy, I beg you. Please... please stop my brother.","117":"Please make him stop tormenting Bern and the people of other regions any further.","118":"Even if it means appealing to the sword?","119":"...Ever since I entrusted everything to Lord Roy, I've made up my mind to it.","120":"Understood. I will definitely stop King Zephiel!","121":"I swear it on the \"Fire Emblem\" entrusted to me by the princess!"};
